# Hard times: want, hurt and the Watch in everyday talk (phase 7, the h7_ lines). Broad scenes anyone might have about
# the times (the dole queue, the cost of living, debts, the Watch, the cold), then scenes for the poor and the
# comfortable, the hungry, the roofless, the hurt, those who fought, and the Watch on duty. Lines in parallel answer
# each other.

## The times, for anyone

scene h7_times_dole_queue
when topic=smalltalk|day
a : The queue for #dole# went right round the chapel this morning. | Did you see the line at the chapel door? For bread. | More folk on #dole# every week. | I saw a wolf I know in the bread line. Pretended I didn't.
b : Round the chapel? It never used to. | I saw. Didn't count. Couldn't bear to. | It's the winter coming. | Best thing. Let them keep their pride.
a : It does now. | Forty, I made it. | It's always coming, for some. | What pride's left.
b : Bad times. | Forty mouths. | Always. | It's all they've got some days.

scene h7_times_bread_dear
when topic=smalltalk|day
a : A loaf costs what two did when I was young. | Bread's dearer and the loaves are smaller. Have you noticed? | I bought half a loaf today. Half! Like a pauper. | They're putting chaff in the bread. I can taste it.
b : When you were young, there were dragons. | Smaller and dearer. That's progress. | Half's better than none. | Chaff's filling. Look on the bright side.
a : There were not. There were cheap loaves. | Progress for the baker. | Half's half. | There's no bright side to chaff.
b : Same thing, near enough. | Ask the baker why. | Better than the bread line. | Then dip it in soup.

scene h7_times_debt
when topic=smalltalk|day
a : Never lend money to a friend. You lose both. | Half this street owes the other half. | Everybody owes somebody. It all goes round in a circle. | The moneylender's got a new coat. Wonder whose that was.
b : Never borrow either. Then you've only enemies. | And the other half owes the Houses. | And the circle's getting smaller. | Ours, probably.
a : Ha. True enough. | And the Houses owe nobody. | Tighter every year. | Ours and our neighbours'.
b : Lonely, but rich. | Funny how that works. | Like a noose. | It's a big coat.

scene h7_times_could_be_worse
when topic=smalltalk|day|friends
a : Could be worse. | At least it's not raining. Inside the house, I mean. | We've a roof and a fire. That's more than some. | Nobody's dead this week. That I know of.
b : Don't say that. It hears you. | Not yet. | And a pot with something in it. | Give it till Restday.
a : What does? | The roof's on its last legs. | Something. Mostly water. | That's grim.
b : Whatever's listening. It always hears. | Then we'll get wet. | Water's a start. | Grim keeps you ready.

scene h7_times_watch_useless
when topic=smalltalk|day
a : Where's #watch# when you want them? | #watch# walked right past a fight last night. | You can't find a guard for love nor money. | They've two guards for the whole market today.
b[guard] #guard : Here. Every day. Mostly being shouted at.
b : Drinking, I expect. | Too many to stop alone, maybe. | Try money. Works better than love. | Two's plenty, if they're quick.
a@guard : Well. Not you. You're one of the good ones.
a : That's my point. | Then call more. | I've neither. | They're not quick.
b@guard : Tell the captain. Loudly.
b : Then don't want them. | They'd have to want to come. | Then you get no guard. | Then we're on our own.
cooldown 1d

scene h7_times_winter_coming
when topic=smalltalk|weather|day here.season=autumn|winter
a : Winter will thin the poor out again. | Folk are already burning furniture down my end. | They'll find someone frozen in a doorway before the thaw. They always do. | I've put by wood for a month. It won't last two weeks.
b : Don't say it like that. | Furniture burns fast. | Every year. And every year we're shocked. | Then come and share ours.
a : How else is there to say it? | Then they burn the floor. | We shouldn't be. | You've hardly any.
b : Kindly. Say it kindly. | Gods help them. | We should, and we are. | Hardly any's some. Two fires cost more than one.
cooldown 1d

scene h7_times_honest_work
when topic=smalltalk|work|day
a : There's no honest work going. Ask anyone. | They took on two at the yard and fifty came. | I'd scrub floors if anyone wanted floors scrubbed. | Work's like hen's teeth this season.
b : There's plenty. It just doesn't pay. | Fifty! For two! | Nobody can afford a clean floor. | Hens have no teeth.
a : Then it's not work, it's a pastime. | And the two were cousins of the foreman. | Or a dirty one. | That's my point.
b : A dear pastime. | Course they were. | It's not the floors, it's the coin. | Ah. I see it now.

scene h7_times_sickness
when topic=smalltalk|day
a : There's a cough going round the poor streets. | Half the street's poorly. | Somebody's pups have the fever. Not ours, thank the gods. | Eat your greens, they say. What greens?
b : There always is, when the cold comes. | And the other half's tired of nursing. | Thank the gods quietly. | Nettles. Free and nasty.
a : The healers can't keep up. | Exactly. | Quietly, then. | Nasty's right.
b : Then keep warm and keep away. | It's a long season. | They'll hear you anyway. | Better than nothing.

## The poor among themselves

scene h7_poor_share
when topic=smalltalk|friends|day a.wealth=poor|destitute b.wealth=poor|destitute
a : I've half a loaf. Want the other half of the half? | Here. It's not much. Take it. | We've turnips. Too many. Have some. | I found two eggs. One's yours.
b : I couldn't. | I'll pay you back. | Too many turnips? Never heard of it. | You found them? Where?
a : You could. You will. | Don't. You'll need it. | Take them before I change my mind. | Don't ask, then you can't tell.
b : Then I'll owe you. | Then I'll pay you in turnips. | Thank you. Truly. | I'm asking nothing.
cooldown 2d

scene h7_poor_tips
when topic=smalltalk|day a.wealth=poor|destitute b.wealth=poor|destitute
a : Baker throws out the burnt ends at dusk. Get there early. | The chapel gives soup on Restday if you sit through the sermon. | The tanner pays a penny for dogs' leavings. Don't ask. | Go to the market late. They'd rather give it than carry it.
b : Early's when everyone gets there. | I'll sit through anything for soup. | I wasn't going to. I am now. | Late. I'll try.
a : Earlier, then. | The sermon's long. | It's a penny. | Smile at the fishwives. They're soft.
b : I'll sleep there. | The soup's thin. | A penny's a penny. | I'll smile. Gods help me.
cooldown 2d

scene h7_poor_dream
when topic=smalltalk|friends a.wealth=poor|destitute b.wealth=poor|destitute
a : If I had a silver coin, do you know what I'd do? | When I'm rich I'll have meat every day. Every day. | One day I'll have boots that don't let the wet in. | If I won a fortune, I'd buy a feather bed and never get up.
b : Spend it on bread, like a fool. | Meat on Restday, at least. | Dry paws. Imagine. | Never?
a : I'd look at it. For a week. | Every day. Twice on Restday. | I can't. | Maybe for meat.
b : Then spend it on bread. | You'd be sick of it. | Neither can I. | Of course.
cooldown 2d

scene h7_poor_pride
when topic=smalltalk|day a.wealth=poor|destitute
a : I'll not go on #dole#. I'll not. | I sold my mother's comb today. | I've been wearing the same coat four winters. | I walked past the bread line twice before I joined it.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #same : Nor would I. Then I did. You get used to it.
b : Pride's cold comfort. | She'd understand. | It's a good coat. | And you joined it. That's what counts.
a@same : I don't want to get used to it.
a : It's what I've got. | She'd scold me. | It was. | It doesn't feel like it.
b@same : Nobody wants to. Come with me tomorrow. We'll stand together.
b : Then keep it. Just eat as well. | Scolding's love. | Still is. | It will.
cooldown 2d

## The comfortable and the rich, to the poor

scene h7_rich_advice
when topic=smalltalk|day a.wealth=rich b.wealth=poor|destitute
a : Have you thought of simply working harder? | You should put a little by each week. It mounts up. | One really ought to avoid debt. It's ruinous. | Bread's not so very dear, surely?
b : Have you thought of shutting up? | A little of nothing mounts to nothing. | So's being poor. | It is, surely.
a : I only meant it kindly. | Then a little less nothing. | One does what one can. | I hadn't noticed.
b : I know. That's the worst of it. | I'll try that. | One does. | No. You wouldn't.
cooldown 2d

scene h7_rich_kind
when topic=smalltalk|friends|day a.wealth=rich|comfortable b.wealth=poor|destitute pair.band=friends|family
a : I had too much from the market. Take some home. | My coat's too small now. It'd fit you. Go on. | I need someone to mind the house tomorrow. I'll pay. Don't argue. | You'll eat with us tonight. That's not a question.
b : You're a bad liar. | It's not too small. | Mind the house? It minds itself. | You keep doing this.
a : I'm a generous liar. | It is now. | It's lonely. It needs company. | And you keep coming. Good.
b : Thank you. I mean it. | ... Thank you. | Then I'll mind it. | I'll bring the bread. What there is.
cooldown 2d

scene h7_rich_cold
when topic=smalltalk|day a.wealth=rich warmth=cold b.wealth=poor|destitute
a : There are too many beggars about. Something ought to be done. | The parish feeds them and they breed. | One can hardly walk without being asked for a penny. | I give to the chapel. That's quite enough.
b : I'm one penny off a beggar. | They eat, too. Imagine. | Then walk somewhere else. | I'm sure the chapel's very grateful.
a : That's not what I meant. | You know what I mean. | I've every right to walk here. | It is. It sends a letter.
b : It's what you said. | I do. That's the trouble. | So have they. | Lovely. Can I eat it?
cooldown 2d

scene h7_owes_lender
when topic=smalltalk|day a.owes=yes
a : I owe more than I'll earn this year. | They've added interest again. On the interest. | I'm hiding from the lender. If they ask, I went to sea. | I borrowed to pay the debt. Now I owe twice.
b : Then earn it next year. | That's how they get you. | You can't swim. | That's how it goes, then down you go.
a : I owe that too. | I know that now. | They don't know that. | I'm already down.
b : Then the year after. | Too late, you mean. | Good. Keep it so. | Then you can only go up.
cooldown 2d

scene h7_owes_to_friend
when topic=smalltalk|friends pair.owed=a|b pair.band=friends|family|acquaintances
a : About that money. | I've not forgotten what's owed. | I know, I know. The money. | We should talk about what's owed.
b : I didn't say anything. | Good. | Did I mention it? | Should we?
a : You didn't have to. | Restday. I swear it. | Your face did. | Not today. Another day.
b : My face is very rude. | Restday, then. | My face apologises. | Another day, then. Soon.
cooldown 2d

## Hungry, and roofless

scene h7_hungry_smell
when topic=smalltalk|day a.hungry=yes
a : Can you smell that? Pies. Somewhere. | When did I last eat? Yesterday? The day before? | My belly's making noises like a cart on cobbles. | I could eat the boards off a barn.
b : That's the cook-shop. Don't torture yourself. | You don't know? | I heard it from here. | You'd get splinters.
a : Too late. | Don't laugh. I can't remember. | It won't stop. | I'd eat the splinters.
b : Here. It's only a crust. | Then eat something now. Here. | Have my heel of bread. | Come on. I'll find you something.
cooldown 1d

scene h7_hungry_child
when topic=smalltalk|family|day a.stage=young|adolescent a.hungry=yes b.stage=adult|old
a : Is there anything to eat? Anything? | My belly hurts. | Can we have supper early? Just this once? | I'm so hungry I could eat the cat.
b : Soon, pup. Soon. | Drink some water. It helps. | There's no early tonight. | Leave the cat be.
a : That's what you said before. | It doesn't. | Why not? | The cat's fat. I'm not.
b : And I meant it then too. | It helps a little. | Because there's nothing early. | I know. Come here.
cooldown 1d

scene h7_homeless_where
when topic=smalltalk|day|friends a.homeless=yes b.homeless=no
a : Where did you sleep last night? I was under the bridge. | The chapel porch is taken. Every night now. | They moved me on twice last night. | Found a dry doorway. Dry, mind. That's a palace.
b : Not under the bridge. It's too wet. | Taken by who? | Who did? | A palace with a draught.
a : Wet's all there is. | Others like me. More every night. | #watch#. Polite, though. | All palaces have draughts.
b : Come to mine. The floor's yours. | Gods. | Polite doesn't keep you warm. | I've heard. Stay at mine tonight.
cooldown 1d

scene h7_homeless_guard
when topic=smalltalk|day a.role=guard b.homeless=yes
a : You can't sleep in this doorway. You know that. | Move along, now. Not here. | Find somewhere off the street before the night watch comes. | Have you anywhere to go tonight?
b : Where, then? Show me where. | Where's along? | You are the night watch. | No.
a : I don't make the rules. | Anywhere I'm not. | I'm the evening watch. They're worse. | ... Try the chapel. Tell them I sent you.
b : You just keep them. | Then I'll go where you aren't. | Gods help me, then. | Will they listen?
a : I do. I'm sorry. | Good. | Go on. Quick. | They might. Go on.
cooldown 1d

## Hurt, and after a fight

scene h7_hurt_bad_ask
when topic=smalltalk|day|friends a.injured=bad
a : Don't touch me. Don't even look too hard. | I can't lift my arm. Look. | I'll be abed a week, the healer says. A week! | Every breath's a knife.
b : What happened to you? | Who did that? | A week's nothing. Heal. | Then breathe small.
a : I fell. That's my story. | A wolf I owed. | I've no week to spare. | That's what I'm doing.
b : Some fall. | Then they'll answer to me. | Nobody does. Take it anyway. | Smaller. Good.
priority 1
cooldown 12h

scene h7_hurt_healer_scold
when topic=smalltalk|day a.injured=light|bad b.job=healer
a : It's only a scratch. | I'll be right as rain tomorrow. | Do you have something for the pain? Something strong? | I tied it up myself. Looks fine, doesn't it?
b : Scratches don't bleed like that. Come here. | Not if you keep walking on it. | Something. Not strong. You'd sleep a week. | It looks like a pudding. Sit down.
a : Ow. Ow! | Fine. Fine. | Then something medium. | It's a good pudding.
b : That's how it heals. | Sit. | Medium. And no ale. | It's a terrible pudding. Hold still.
cooldown 12h

scene h7_fought_who_won
when topic=smalltalk|day|friends a.fought=yes
a : I was in a fight. Don't laugh. | You should see the other one. Well, you shouldn't. They're fine. | I hit somebody. I've never hit anybody. | Somebody went for me. I bit them.
b : Who won? | So you lost. | How did it feel? | Bit them? Where?
a : Nobody. We both fell over. | I lost very well. | Horrible. Then good. Then horrible. | I'll not say. They'll not sit for a week.
b : Then it was a draw. | Losing well's still losing. | That sounds about right. | Ha! Good.
cooldown 12h

scene h7_fought_short_temper
when topic=smalltalk|day a.fought=yes a.temper=short
a : They had it coming. They know it. | I'd do it again. Twice. | Nobody talks to me like that. Nobody. | If they come back, I'll finish it.
b : Nobody has it coming like that. | Then you'd be in #gaol# twice. | Somebody just did. And you hit them. | Finish what? You'll finish in the cells.
a : You weren't there. | Worth it. | They'll think twice. | Then I'll finish there.
b : No. But I'm here now. Calm down. | It never is. | So will #watch#. | You're a fool. A brave fool.
cooldown 12h

scene h7_fighting_now
when topic=smalltalk|day|quarrel a.fighting=yes
a : Stay back! | Get out of the way! | Not now! | Mind yourself!
b : Gods! I'm going! | Stop it, both of you! | I'll fetch #watch#! | Stop! Stop!
a : Go! | Back! | Go on, then! | Back!
b : I'm gone. | I'm fetching them! | Running! | Stop it!
priority 2

## The Watch on duty

scene h7_watch_night_round
when topic=smalltalk|day|work a.on_watch=yes b.on_watch=yes here.time=night
a : All quiet your end? | Saw a light in the old store. Turned out to be a cat with a candle. | Cold one tonight. | Nothing yet. I hate nothing. Nothing's waiting.
b : Quiet as a grave. | A cat with a candle? | Bitter. My ears are numb. | Nothing's nothing. Enjoy it.
a : Don't say grave on the night round. | Well. Near the candle. | Keep your hood up. | I'll enjoy it when it's dawn.
b : Quiet as a pillow, then. | Close enough. | And my tail in. | Dawn's three hours yet.
cooldown 1d

scene h7_watch_pay
when topic=work|smalltalk a.role=guard b.role=guard
a : Pay's late again. | They want us on double rounds for the same coin. | My boots have holes, and the captain says buy new. With what? | I've not been paid since the last market day.
b : It always is. | Same coin, half the sleep. | With the money we're not paid. | Nobody has. They say next week.
a : I've rent due. | We should say something. | Exactly. | They said that last week.
b : Tell your landlord you're keeping the peace. | Say it, then. I'll stand behind you. Far behind. | Stuff them with straw. | And next week they'll say it again.
cooldown 2d

scene h7_watch_civilian_thanks
when topic=smalltalk|day a.role=civilian b.on_watch=yes
a : Long night, was it? | Thank you for walking our street. | Anything I should know about? | Here. It's warm. Drink it.
b : Long enough. | It's the job. | Nothing for your ears. Lock your door. | You're kind. I'll not refuse.
a : You look it. | It's still kind of you. | That's what you always say. | I'll not ask what's in it.
b : Thank you very much. | Kind's not the job. Still. Thank you. | Because it's always true. | Nothing you'd not drink yourself.
cooldown 1d

scene h7_watch_bribe
when topic=smalltalk|day a.honesty=sly b.on_watch=yes
a : If a wolf wanted a door left unwatched, what would that cost? | You look thirsty. Here's a penny for a drink. No reason. | Busy night ahead? Which streets? | Do you ever look the other way? For a friend?
b : Your head. | I'll drink it. And remember your face. | Ask me again. I dare you. | I've no friends. Not on duty.
a : Only asking. Idly. | It's a friendly face! | I'm only asking for my safety. | Shame.
b : Ask idly somewhere else. | I'll remember it all the same. | Then stay in. Safe. | I'm full of shame. Move along.
cooldown 2d
